1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,162
WWW.MY-SUBS.CO

﻿1
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:09,320
(BELL RINGS)

2
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:02,680
Oh. Hello, Edith, dear.

3
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:05,040
Hello, Granny. Isn't it exciting?

4
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:07,920
At my age one must ration one's excitement.

5
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:10,120
Oh.

6
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:14,520
I told her everything would come
right but she wouldn't believe me.

7
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,480
I still can't.

8
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:19,360
Something happening in this
house is actually about me.

9
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:21,080
The dress came this morning.

10
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:24,480
I was sad you decided against Patou.
I would've paid.

11
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:28,920
Lucile was safer. We don't want
her to look like a chorus girl.

12
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:32,360
How's Anthony? Excited,
I hope. Desperately.

13
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:34,920
Just when he thought his
life would never change,

14
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:39,320
he's going back to the beginning.
What an invigorating prospect!

15
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:43,400
I hope you've got your
shirt ready for tonight.

16
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:47,360
I've hidden a couple so I won't
be  caught out that way again.

17
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:51,040
Why should I be interested?
That goes for you, too. Me?

18
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:53,120
Take no notice.

19
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:56,360
Anna, are the flowers done?

20
00:01:56,360 --> 00:02:00,480
Yes, I'll check them on Saturday
and lose any that's going over.

21
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:04,000
I've kept back a few in bud. I'll
be home for the dressing gong.

22
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,920
We'll manage.

23
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,000
Still no word from the doctor?

24
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,560
I'd have told you if there was.

25
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:15,840
They don't mind stringing it
out. Shall we got and see him?

26
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:19,760
Why? I'm sure if he knew
anything he would've said.

27
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,960
How are you today, Mr Molesley?

28
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,680
Oh.

29
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,880
Very well, thank you.

30
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:31,920
You were talking the other night
 about your friend's daughter.

31
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:34,200
Is she still looking for a place? She is.

32
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:38,080
You read about the servant
shortage in the newspapers

33
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:42,120
but you can't find a situation
for a lady's maid. Not one.

34
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:45,440
She'll end up as a house
maid if she's not careful.

35
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:49,480
We can't have that. If I
were  to tell you something,

36
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:52,160
promise not to breathe  a word downstairs.

37
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:55,160
Miss O'Brien doesn't want  anyone to know.

38
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,800
How will they advertise it?

39
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,800
I don't know exactly.

40
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:09,080
Desirable nobleman's mansion

41
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,440
with surrounding estate and properties.

44
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:20,920
The house is pretty, we
might make something of it.

45
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:24,280
We could rename it Downton
Place. Who lives there now?

46
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,760
A tenant but we can come to an arrangement.

47
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:30,960
Let's take a picnic there tomorrow
on Edith's last day of freedom.

48
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:34,320
Molesley's in the hall.
Would you have a word?

49
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:37,800
I'll come through in a minute.
Not with you, with Mama.

50
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:40,040
Molesley.

51
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:46,640
Your Ladyship, may I have a word?

52
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:48,360
Of course.

53
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:53,960
My Lady, might I be allowed
 to put forward a candidate

54
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:56,800
as Miss O'Brien's replacement? What?

55
00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:00,120
When the time comes. Is O'Brien leaving?

56
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,760
I hope I've not spoken out of turn,

57
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:07,520
only I didn't want to miss
the chance. I thought you knew.

58
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:10,960
Of course I know, thank
you. I'll be happy to listen

59
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:13,760
to recommendations when the time comes.

60
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:16,080
Thank you, My Lady.

61
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:22,800
Well, I must confess, I'll watch
her departure with mixed emotions.

62
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:26,840
Mine are fairly unmixed. Did
you have a clue? Not a clue.

63
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:29,200
How very disappointing.

64
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:33,560
In a way it raises the big
question when do we tell the staff

65
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:36,000
that the end is nigh? It sounds so final.

66
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,320
I'm afraid it is final.

67
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,400
Well, don't spoil Edith's stay.

68
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:44,520
Let's get through the wedding
first then tell them afterwards.

69
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:49,360
Oh, Dr Clarkson.

70
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:53,680
Do you have a minute? Er, one minute, yes.

71
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:56,880
Do you mind if we... Only I know Mrs Hughes

72
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:59,040
is suffering from a condition

73
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:02,560
and I wondered if there's
anything I can do to help?

74
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:05,440
You can help by lessening her duties.

75
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:09,400
But you can't tell me how
serious it is? I'm afraid not.

76
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,720
Even if I knew, which I don't...

77
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,480
yet.

78
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,480
Good day to you, Mr Carson.

79
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:20,760
I had a telephone call
from Charkham earlier.

80
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:23,680
Charkham? Reggie Swire's lawyer.

81
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:26,200
The death certificate
has arrived from India.

82
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:30,360
He wants to bring it here. Can't
he send it? He wants to bring it.

83
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,400
He was quite definite.

84
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:36,320
I told him to come tomorrow.
There's nothing going on, is there?

85
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:39,440
You know there is, we're taking a picnic

86
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:42,280
to see the house we have to move into.

87
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:46,120
I'm surprised you, of all
people, can forget that. (SIGHS)

88
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:49,760
He's coming in the morning,
I won't put him off. Oh.

89
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:53,920
This is the moment when you receive
a huge fortune that could save Downton

90
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,960
and you give it away?

91
00:05:57,160 --> 00:06:00,920
Will you choose where to
give it? I'd give it to Papa!

92
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:05,800
I hope in some small part of you you
can understand. I'm trying, really.

93
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:08,680
But I can't pretend I'm doing very well.

94
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:12,360
(DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES)

95
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:15,480
Will there be anything more, My Lady?

96
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,200
No.

97
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:22,200
Unless you have something
you want to tell me.

98
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,280
What might that be, My Lady?

99
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:28,760
I won't prompt you, O'Brien,
if you're not ready to say.

100
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:38,720
Did she tell you why? No.

101
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:43,360
Maybe she won't till she settles

102
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:46,480
where she's going but she has let me down.

103
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:51,120
We should go. Strallan won't be
late. He never is, worse luck. Oh.

104
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:53,480
I know you're not happy,

105
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:55,800
but Edith will be in the same county.

106
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:59,800
Loxley's a nice house, the
estate will give her plenty to do.

107
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:02,720
She'll be a nurse and by the time she's 50

108
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:05,880
she'll be wheeling
round a one-arm OLD man.

109
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:12,480
Are you waiting till they come
in search of the pudding? No.

110
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:22,280
Can I do something for you?
I'd better get back upstairs,

111
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:24,840
but, um, while you're here,

112
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:28,640
I saw Dr Clarkson today.

113
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:31,160
Oh?

114
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:33,680
I'm worried about Mrs Hughes.

115
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:36,400
We're all worried,

116
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:38,840
but I don't think he should've told you.

117
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:42,520
He said it would help if
we lessened her workload.

118
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:47,240
I'm sure it would but she won't
be pleased he's talked about her

119
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:49,240
before it's been confirmed.

120
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:54,800
So it is cancer? Not until it's confirmed.

121
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:58,800
Don't say anything. She'd hate
to think the doctor told you.

122
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:02,160
He didn't tell me, Mrs Patmore,

123
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:05,520
you told me.

124
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:10,400
(SIGHS)

125
00:08:18,434 --> 00:08:23,674
Dear Edith... Edith tells me
you're very interested in politics.

126
00:08:23,674 --> 00:08:25,914
Tom is our tame revolutionary.

127
00:08:25,914 --> 00:08:27,994
Every family should have one.

128
00:08:27,994 --> 00:08:29,954
As long as you are tame.

129
00:08:29,954 --> 00:08:32,434
Tame enough for a game of billiards.

130
00:08:32,434 --> 00:08:34,394
What about it?

131
00:08:36,834 --> 00:08:39,234
Can you tell them where we've gone?

132
00:08:46,314 --> 00:08:50,034
We're getting used to Tom
and I hope you will, too.

133
00:08:51,114 --> 00:08:54,874
We haven't spoken, really,
since it was all settled.

134
00:08:54,874 --> 00:08:58,714
I want you to know I quite
understand why you were against it.

135
00:08:58,714 --> 00:09:01,034
Yes. Well...

136
00:09:01,034 --> 00:09:05,434
I hope you believe I'll do my
best to make her happy. I do.

137
00:09:05,434 --> 00:09:07,994
It was never personal. No, of course not.

138
00:09:07,994 --> 00:09:12,554
No, it's just because of
all this and I'm far too old.

139
00:09:12,554 --> 00:09:16,114
The thing is done, there's
no point raking it over.

140
00:09:16,114 --> 00:09:18,994
But are you happy about it?

141
00:09:18,994 --> 00:09:23,234
I'm happy Edith is happy, I'm
happy you mean to keep her happy.

142
00:09:23,234 --> 00:09:25,914
That's enough happiness
to be going on with.

143
00:09:28,514 --> 00:09:32,554
There's been a last-minute change
of mind about the wedding menus.

144
00:09:32,554 --> 00:09:36,434
Couldn't Mrs Patmore do it?
She's given me her new order list.

145
00:09:36,434 --> 00:09:38,914
She's done her job, it's
time for me to do mine.

146
00:09:38,914 --> 00:09:41,154
I don't want you to get tired.

147
00:09:41,554 --> 00:09:43,674
Who have you been speaking to?

148
00:09:44,114 --> 00:09:46,914
No-one. What do you mean?

149
00:09:46,914 --> 00:09:51,034
Nothing. I don't mean a
thing. Now, let me get on.

150
00:09:53,674 --> 00:09:58,674
This is a simple stitch but
strong and very useful in a drama.

151
00:09:58,674 --> 00:10:00,714
When do we get summat to eat?

152
00:10:00,714 --> 00:10:03,514
As I was saying, you should start it

153
00:10:03,514 --> 00:10:06,754
about half an inch away
from the centre line.

154
00:10:08,634 --> 00:10:10,834
Oh, I'm glad you've come back.

155
00:10:11,634 --> 00:10:13,954
I do hope you've come for our help.

156
00:10:13,954 --> 00:10:16,514
You'd be so welcome if you have.

157
00:10:16,514 --> 00:10:19,514
You wouldn't say that
if you knew what I am.

158
00:10:19,514 --> 00:10:22,034
I'm past help. Nobody's past help.

159
00:10:22,034 --> 00:10:25,834
If you mean you're a
prostitute, you should know

160
00:10:25,834 --> 00:10:30,074
it is true of every woman who has
come here to rebuild their lives.

161
00:10:30,074 --> 00:10:34,114
I'm helping them and I hope I
can help you, too. That's right.

162
00:10:34,114 --> 00:10:38,514
Why not come in and help us
rebuild our lives? (LAUGHTER)

163
00:10:38,514 --> 00:10:40,274
That's not why I'm here.

164
00:10:41,394 --> 00:10:44,034
That is, I am a... what you said

165
00:10:44,874 --> 00:10:49,034
but I don't want help, not for myself,

166
00:10:49,034 --> 00:10:51,754
but...

167
00:10:51,754 --> 00:10:55,474
When I make up my mind... I'm
sorry, this has been a mistake.

168
00:10:55,474 --> 00:10:59,114
Please, please, don't
go, not again. (LAUGHTER)

169
00:10:59,114 --> 00:11:03,114
It must be strange to receive
a letter from a dead man.

170
00:11:04,034 --> 00:11:05,914
It's very strange.

171
00:11:06,554 --> 00:11:08,634
We're leaving.

172
00:11:08,634 --> 00:11:11,514
I'm sorry, Mr Charkham, to snatch him away.

173
00:11:11,514 --> 00:11:16,394
That's quite all right, Lady
Mary. There will be papers to sign.

174
00:11:16,394 --> 00:11:18,394
Yes, I expect there will.

175
00:11:25,074 --> 00:11:27,874
Papa's asked Anthony to meet us there

176
00:11:27,874 --> 00:11:30,034
so we can all face the future together.

177
00:11:30,034 --> 00:11:32,314
He's bringing Isobel and Granny.

178
00:11:32,314 --> 00:11:36,554
It's hard for your grandmother.
It's torture for all of us,

179
00:11:36,554 --> 00:11:40,474
and if I ever look like I'm
finding it easy to lose my home

180
00:11:40,474 --> 00:11:42,634
then I am putting on act.

181
00:11:49,514 --> 00:11:52,194
Are you sure you can
manage this? Quite sure.

182
00:11:52,194 --> 00:11:55,114
It's nothing hot. It's
not a shooting lunch.

183
00:11:55,114 --> 00:11:59,194
Give them Champagne. That'll allow
you time to set it out properly.

184
00:11:59,194 --> 00:12:02,234
I'll manage. What's this
place we're visiting?

185
00:12:02,234 --> 00:12:06,754
One of His Lordship's houses. I
wonder why they're going there today.

186
00:12:06,754 --> 00:12:09,514
Maybe he likes to keep
a check on things. Maybe.

187
00:12:09,514 --> 00:12:11,754
See you there. Off you go.

188
00:12:12,354 --> 00:12:15,234
She was a cousin of Granny's.

189
00:12:15,514 --> 00:12:17,834
Do you want to come with us? Yes.

190
00:12:17,834 --> 00:12:20,114
Thank you. Might I have a word, My Lady?

191
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:24,154
Of course. What is it? This
is a slightly awkward request,

192
00:12:24,154 --> 00:12:26,834
what with the wedding tomorrow... Tell me.

193
00:12:26,834 --> 00:12:30,474
Mrs Hughes is very tired.

194
00:12:30,474 --> 00:12:34,514
I wonder if it might be possible
to divert some of her work my way?

195
00:12:34,514 --> 00:12:37,234
I don't understand. What do you mean tired?

196
00:12:37,234 --> 00:12:39,074
Cora...

197
00:12:39,074 --> 00:12:40,794
Carson?

198
00:12:40,794 --> 00:12:43,954
The fact is Mrs Hughes is ill,

199
00:12:43,954 --> 00:12:46,274
My Lady. She may be very ill.

200
00:12:47,114 --> 00:12:49,794
I'm extremely sorry to
trouble you with this

201
00:12:49,794 --> 00:12:53,354
at such a moment, but I don't
want the wedding to sink her.

202
00:12:53,354 --> 00:12:55,994
Of course not, but how will we manage

203
00:12:55,994 --> 00:12:58,754
without O'Brien and now Mrs Hughes?

204
00:12:58,754 --> 00:13:03,314
Miss O'Brien? She told
Molesley... Cora, please.

205
00:13:04,274 --> 00:13:05,954
I'm coming.

206
00:13:35,234 --> 00:13:36,954
Mrs Bartlett?

207
00:13:38,194 --> 00:13:40,194
I've brought the money.

208
00:13:48,514 --> 00:13:51,074
It's your loss cos I've got nothing to say.

209
00:13:52,954 --> 00:13:55,434
All I want to know is if Vera ever...

210
00:13:55,434 --> 00:13:59,314
Oh. So you were on Christian
name terms, were you?

211
00:14:00,394 --> 00:14:02,274
You do surprise me.

212
00:14:03,194 --> 00:14:08,914
If Mrs Bates ever suggested
she was depressed or unhappy...

213
00:14:08,914 --> 00:14:10,954
Of course she was unhappy.

214
00:14:10,954 --> 00:14:14,914
Her husband had left her
and gone off with a trollop.

215
00:14:17,554 --> 00:14:22,194
He'd changed, you know. She
was scared of him by the end.

216
00:14:22,194 --> 00:14:24,274
And now we know she had good reason.

217
00:14:24,674 --> 00:14:26,634
When did you last see her?

218
00:14:29,754 --> 00:14:31,754
You'd better come inside.

219
00:14:41,234 --> 00:14:42,954
Bates.

220
00:14:43,474 --> 00:14:45,194
Watch out.

221
00:14:46,834 --> 00:14:50,314
What do you mean? Search
your room, search your bed.

222
00:14:50,314 --> 00:14:53,394
They've set you up, your
cellmate and his mates.

223
00:14:53,394 --> 00:14:55,314
Stop talking!

224
00:14:56,714 --> 00:14:58,634
Just do it.

225
00:15:01,754 --> 00:15:04,034
Her door was open so I looked in.

226
00:15:04,034 --> 00:15:07,834
She was cooking, but
she had to post a letter

227
00:15:07,834 --> 00:15:09,874
so we walked me down the street.

228
00:15:09,874 --> 00:15:13,834
She said Bates was coming
back later for his tea.

229
00:15:13,834 --> 00:15:15,954
She was terrified.

230
00:15:15,954 --> 00:15:18,674
She was in a strange mood,

231
00:15:18,674 --> 00:15:21,154
jumpy, fearful,

232
00:15:21,154 --> 00:15:23,034
but determined.

233
00:15:24,034 --> 00:15:26,954
She'd made pastry, she
scrubbed it out of her nails

234
00:15:26,954 --> 00:15:29,514
like she didn't care if
she took the skin off.

235
00:15:29,794 --> 00:15:33,554
So after she posted the letter
she went home on her own?

236
00:15:34,834 --> 00:15:39,234
She did, poor soul, and
I never saw her after.

237
00:15:40,754 --> 00:15:44,914
I can remember her now
walking away down the street.

238
00:15:44,914 --> 00:15:48,314
It was raining. No, not
raining, more like drizzle.

239
00:15:48,314 --> 00:15:52,274
The gaslight seemed to make
a sort of halo around her.

240
00:15:52,274 --> 00:15:54,914
A halo? Really?

241
00:15:54,914 --> 00:15:57,554
You can laugh.

242
00:15:57,554 --> 00:15:59,674
When did you hear she was dead?

243
00:15:59,674 --> 00:16:01,394
Next day.

244
00:16:01,994 --> 00:16:04,234
Somehow, I knew it was Bates.

245
00:16:04,234 --> 00:16:07,314
When I heard the verdict,
I thought he'd swing.

246
00:16:08,434 --> 00:16:11,794
He should've if the
country hadn't gone soft.

247
00:16:11,794 --> 00:16:13,794
(CRIES)

248
00:16:16,354 --> 00:16:19,914
This is very good of you.
Nonsense, we were on the way.

249
00:16:19,914 --> 00:16:24,154
I wish you'd let me sit in the
front. I prefer it, I've ridden

250
00:16:24,154 --> 00:16:27,794
in the front seat many times.
Aren't you a wild thing!

251
00:16:27,794 --> 00:16:32,474
There's never been a safer method
of travel. Nor a faster one.

252
00:16:32,474 --> 00:16:36,554
Edith's the speed fiend, she
likes to go at a terrific lick.

253
00:16:36,554 --> 00:16:40,314
Do you think you'll be able
to keep up with her? I'll try.

254
00:16:40,314 --> 00:16:43,914
What's this place like? Do you know it?

255
00:16:43,914 --> 00:16:47,434
A little. My late husband
kept the shooting there.

256
00:16:47,434 --> 00:16:51,194
We'd sometimes have luncheon
in the house. Is it nice?

257
00:16:51,194 --> 00:16:54,074
Nice enough, as a retreat from the world.

258
00:16:54,074 --> 00:16:57,514
I wouldn't have thought
it suited to much else.

259
00:17:06,074 --> 00:17:07,874
Downton Place.

260
00:17:09,754 --> 00:17:11,474
How lovely.

261
00:17:15,194 --> 00:17:20,234
Won't it be a bit cramped?  For most
 people it looks like a fairy palace.

262
00:17:20,234 --> 00:17:23,914
We'll be able to run it
with a much smaller staff.

263
00:17:23,914 --> 00:17:27,354
This is it. We won't need
more than eight servants, tops.

264
00:17:27,354 --> 00:17:29,954
So it'll be very economical. It...

265
00:17:33,114 --> 00:17:35,354
What about me? Where am I to go?

266
00:17:35,354 --> 00:17:40,114
We still own most of the village.
Oh. Perhaps I could open a shop?

267
00:17:40,114 --> 00:17:43,554
Good idea, Granny. What
do you think it needs?

268
00:17:43,554 --> 00:17:48,154
If it's like everywhere else, good
manners and decent conversation.

269
00:17:48,154 --> 00:17:51,434
Then you should have a
roaring trade in minutes.

270
00:17:52,794 --> 00:17:55,154
How's everything going? Very well.

271
00:17:55,154 --> 00:17:58,194
It's unfair Mary had an
archbishop to marry her

272
00:17:58,194 --> 00:18:00,554
and you've got poor old Mr Travis.

273
00:18:00,554 --> 00:18:03,954
I don't mind, it's such short
notice, he was booked up.

274
00:18:03,954 --> 00:18:08,434
I prefer it, really, to have
the man who christened us. Hm.

275
00:18:09,314 --> 00:18:11,314
What did Charkham come for?

276
00:18:12,434 --> 00:18:14,754
He gave me a letter from Swire.

277
00:18:15,514 --> 00:18:18,874
He left one for each of
the three potential heirs

278
00:18:18,874 --> 00:18:20,994
when and if they inherited.

279
00:18:20,994 --> 00:18:23,714
Mine is the only one
to have been delivered.

280
00:18:23,714 --> 00:18:25,634
What did it say?

281
00:18:25,634 --> 00:18:27,594
I haven't opened it.

282
00:18:28,634 --> 00:18:30,794
I can't decide whether I will.

283
00:18:30,794 --> 00:18:34,834
Why wouldn't you? Because I
know it'll be a paean of praise,

284
00:18:34,834 --> 00:18:39,354
how Lavinia could not have
found a better man, etc.

285
00:18:39,354 --> 00:18:43,394
And you don't want to read that?
She could not have found a worse one.

286
00:18:43,394 --> 00:18:46,954
No, I don't. I feel bad
enough and if I read his words

287
00:18:46,954 --> 00:18:48,954
they will stay with me forever.

288
00:18:59,154 --> 00:19:00,914
Ah.

289
00:19:00,914 --> 00:19:04,874
Mrs Crawley? We're back
from our delicious luncheon

290
00:19:04,874 --> 00:19:07,634
and I was on my way home.

291
00:19:07,634 --> 00:19:10,954
You had a maid at Downton, Ethel Parks.

292
00:19:10,954 --> 00:19:14,674
I was here when she brought
her son into the dining room.

293
00:19:14,674 --> 00:19:18,354
Who could forget that? Do
you have an address for her?

294
00:19:18,354 --> 00:19:20,874
I do, if she's still there.

295
00:19:20,874 --> 00:19:22,714
You see...

296
00:19:24,594 --> 00:19:27,034
You see, I saw her this morning

297
00:19:27,034 --> 00:19:29,554
and I'm afraid she's fallen into a bad way.

298
00:19:30,394 --> 00:19:32,514
A very bad way. Oh, dear.

299
00:19:32,514 --> 00:19:34,594
I am sorry to hear that.

300
00:19:34,594 --> 00:19:38,594
If you'd like to come with me,
I'll fetch it for you. Thank you.

301
00:19:54,314 --> 00:19:56,394
(KEYS JANGLE)

302
00:20:01,634 --> 00:20:03,634
(KEY TURNS IN LOCK)

303
00:20:04,714 --> 00:20:07,634
Get up, both of you! Against the wall!

304
00:20:07,634 --> 00:20:09,634
Mr Turner, search the bunk, please.

305
00:20:18,274 --> 00:20:20,634
Nothing here. What?

306
00:20:32,954 --> 00:20:34,954
Clean this mess up!

307
00:20:37,194 --> 00:20:39,194
(DOOR IS LOCKED)

308
00:20:43,114 --> 00:20:44,834
Bastards!

309
00:20:49,074 --> 00:20:51,074
There's a lot of bastards in here.

310
00:20:58,114 --> 00:21:01,194
Oh, right. I expect you're tired.

311
00:21:01,194 --> 00:21:03,634
It's a long day up to London  and back.

312
00:21:03,634 --> 00:21:05,914
Worth the journey? Not really.

313
00:21:05,914 --> 00:21:10,554
Miss O'Brien, might I ask what
you've confided in Mr Molesley

314
00:21:10,554 --> 00:21:14,394
but have kept from the rest of
us? I don't know what you mean.

315
00:21:14,394 --> 00:21:18,434
Mr Molesley has given Her Ladyship
the impression you're planning

316
00:21:18,434 --> 00:21:21,034
a change of some sort. What's this?

317
00:21:22,834 --> 00:21:26,274
I'm sorry, I thought
Her Ladyship would know.

318
00:21:26,274 --> 00:21:28,274
Know what?

319
00:21:28,274 --> 00:21:30,314
That you're leaving.

320
00:21:31,554 --> 00:21:33,954
I beg your pardon?

321
00:21:34,634 --> 00:21:37,354
How dare you make such an assumption!

322
00:21:39,154 --> 00:21:42,634
Isn't it time for the
dressing gong, Mr Carson?

323
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:47,114
It certainly is.  But... Excuse me,
Mr Molesley, I've got work to do,

324
00:21:47,114 --> 00:21:49,034
even if you haven't.

325
00:21:50,794 --> 00:21:52,794
I'll deal with you later.

326
00:21:53,994 --> 00:21:58,034
You're in the soup. I wouldn't be
 in her bad books for a gold clock.

327
00:22:10,113 --> 00:22:13,553
You must've said something
Molesley misinterpreted.

328
00:22:13,553 --> 00:22:18,673
I say nothing to him beyond "Pass
the salt" and "Out of the way".

329
00:22:18,673 --> 00:22:20,753
There must have been something.

330
00:22:20,753 --> 00:22:24,233
I do feel let down, and
right on top of the wedding...

331
00:22:24,233 --> 00:22:27,953
(KNOCK ON DOOR) You sent
for me, My Lady. Yes.

332
00:22:28,873 --> 00:22:30,873
Thank you, O'Brien.

333
00:22:35,553 --> 00:22:38,313
Mrs Hughes, I understand
that you're not well.

334
00:22:39,633 --> 00:22:44,993
Whom do you understand that
from? Because if the doctor...

335
00:22:44,993 --> 00:22:46,993
It wasn't Doctor Clarkson.

336
00:22:47,713 --> 00:22:50,793
It is not confirmed that
I am ill, Your Ladyship.

337
00:22:51,473 --> 00:22:55,353
I've had a test and I'm
waiting for the results,

338
00:22:55,353 --> 00:22:57,393
but I am perfectly capable...

339
00:22:57,393 --> 00:23:00,153
Mrs Hughes, I only want to say one thing,

340
00:23:00,153 --> 00:23:04,233
that if you are ill you are welcome
here for as long as you want.

341
00:23:04,233 --> 00:23:09,073
Lady Sybil will help us to
find a suitable nurse. I see.

342
00:23:09,073 --> 00:23:13,113
I don't want you to have
concerns about where you'll go

343
00:23:13,113 --> 00:23:17,353
or who'll look after you. The
answer is here and we will.

344
00:23:20,433 --> 00:23:22,633
I don't know what to say, My Lady.

345
00:23:22,633 --> 00:23:27,473
There's isn't anything more to
say until we know where we stand.

346
00:23:27,473 --> 00:23:29,153
Thank you.

347
00:23:31,753 --> 00:23:34,433
He thinks I don't know
but, of course, I do.

348
00:23:34,433 --> 00:23:38,913
We'll spend two weeks in Rome,
then Florence, then Venice,

349
00:23:38,913 --> 00:23:40,953
so I couldn't be happier.

350
00:23:40,953 --> 00:23:44,993
What about Loxley? Is there masses
to be done? It's not too bad.

351
00:23:44,993 --> 00:23:48,233
It's not too bad downstairs.
The bedrooms are killers.

352
00:23:48,233 --> 00:23:52,593
Don't do anything too fast, it takes
 time to know how a house works.

353
00:23:53,233 --> 00:23:57,873
You really should go to bed.
No bride wants to look tired.

354
00:23:57,873 --> 00:24:01,873
It either means she's
anxious or been up to no good.

355
00:24:01,873 --> 00:24:04,873
I won't sleep a wink. Tonight or tomorrow?

356
00:24:05,473 --> 00:24:08,873
Sybil, vulgarity is no substitute for wit.

357
00:24:08,873 --> 00:24:10,593
You started it.

358
00:24:10,593 --> 00:24:12,233
(GIGGLING)

359
00:24:13,273 --> 00:24:15,193
Miss O'Brien?

360
00:24:15,193 --> 00:24:18,433
Please understand I didn't mean any harm.

361
00:24:18,433 --> 00:24:20,593
Why make it up in the first place?

362
00:24:20,593 --> 00:24:23,153
I didn't make it up, I
was told. Who told you?

363
00:24:23,153 --> 00:24:27,153
Mr Barrow mentioned it, but I
think  it was an honest mistake.

364
00:24:27,153 --> 00:24:31,113
No, it wasn't honest
and it wasn't a mistake,

365
00:24:31,113 --> 00:24:34,873
but don't worry about it, I
can tell it wasn't your fault,

366
00:24:34,873 --> 00:24:36,913
so we'll forget about it, shall we?

367
00:24:36,913 --> 00:24:39,873
And when you see Mr Barrow,

368
00:24:39,873 --> 00:24:44,393
you can tell him I may make
some honest mistakes myself.

369
00:24:44,393 --> 00:24:47,353
No doubt we'll find out.
Probably the hard way.

370
00:24:57,673 --> 00:25:00,553
Why not eat with us?
Oh, I couldn't do that.

371
00:25:00,553 --> 00:25:04,193
Daisy won't sit down, the
invitation is not in your gift.

372
00:25:04,193 --> 00:25:07,073
She eats with Mrs Patmore in the kitchen.

373
00:25:07,073 --> 00:25:09,233
Fancy a game of something later?

374
00:25:10,153 --> 00:25:12,353
Daisy's busy.

375
00:25:12,353 --> 00:25:16,153
Anna? I want to write a letter. Sorry.

376
00:25:16,153 --> 00:25:19,033
I'll play. Let's see how we feel.

377
00:25:21,873 --> 00:25:24,073
What do you mean you've read it?

378
00:25:24,073 --> 00:25:28,113
It wasn't right to destroy a man's
last words without reading them.

379
00:25:28,113 --> 00:25:31,153
It wasn't your decision.
I made it my decision.

380
00:25:31,153 --> 00:25:33,873
Do you want to hear what he says? No.

381
00:25:33,873 --> 00:25:37,033
Lavinia must have written
to him on her last day

382
00:25:37,033 --> 00:25:40,473
hours before she died. Nonsense.
No letter was in her room.

383
00:25:40,473 --> 00:25:44,633
She wrote to him after she tried to
persuade you to call off the wedding.

384
00:25:45,593 --> 00:25:47,593
This is quite impossible.

385
00:25:50,793 --> 00:25:55,113
"She loved and admired you for
the sacrifice of your happiness.

386
00:25:55,113 --> 00:25:57,153
She commended you to my care."

387
00:25:57,153 --> 00:26:00,033
I can't listen to any
more of this. You must.

388
00:26:00,033 --> 00:26:04,113
"I have few intimates so have
added you to my list of heirs.

389
00:26:04,113 --> 00:26:07,073
It's unlikely I'll outlive the first two

390
00:26:07,073 --> 00:26:10,353
so there's little chance
of you reading this.

391
00:26:10,353 --> 00:26:13,113
If you do and the money has come to you,

392
00:26:13,113 --> 00:26:16,153
know it is with my full
knowledge of what transpired.

393
00:26:16,153 --> 00:26:20,153
Do not allow grief, guilt or regret
to hold you back in its employment.

394
00:26:21,033 --> 00:26:25,073
God bless you, my boy. Reggie."

395
00:26:34,113 --> 00:26:36,113
Are you sure you didn't write it?

396
00:26:45,593 --> 00:26:47,753
I'm not accusing you of faking it,

397
00:26:49,593 --> 00:26:51,393
but I suspect someone has.

398
00:26:51,393 --> 00:26:53,513
So it won't change your mind?

399
00:26:53,513 --> 00:26:55,633
Not yet it won't.

400
00:27:03,593 --> 00:27:05,593
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

401
00:27:07,313 --> 00:27:10,433
Time you were in bed.
It's a big day tomorrow.

402
00:27:10,433 --> 00:27:12,753
I'll just finish this.

403
00:27:12,753 --> 00:27:15,233
Is there something I can do for you?

404
00:27:16,393 --> 00:27:18,113
No.

405
00:27:20,673 --> 00:27:25,313
Did you say anything
about me to Her Ladyship?

406
00:27:25,713 --> 00:27:28,513
I don't know what you mean. Why?

407
00:27:28,633 --> 00:27:31,873
Don't worry. She was very kind and...

408
00:27:31,873 --> 00:27:33,713
I was touched.

409
00:27:33,713 --> 00:27:36,673
As you know, I don't worship them all,

410
00:27:36,673 --> 00:27:39,793
like you do. I wouldn't put it like that.

411
00:27:39,793 --> 00:27:43,193
But this time, I freely admit it

412
00:27:44,033 --> 00:27:46,033
I was quite touched.

413
00:28:06,073 --> 00:28:11,553
Am I interrupting? No, please, I
just want to ask you all something.

414
00:28:11,553 --> 00:28:15,753
I'm sorry I've not been up. Don't
worry, I'll change after luncheon.

415
00:28:15,753 --> 00:28:18,393
I had to catch you when
you were all together.

416
00:28:18,393 --> 00:28:21,033
How can we help, My
Lady? It's a funny thing.

417
00:28:21,033 --> 00:28:24,313
Mr Crawley has heard
Miss Swire sent a letter

418
00:28:24,313 --> 00:28:28,433
on the day she died. If so,
someone must have posted it for her

419
00:28:28,433 --> 00:28:30,873
and we wondered if it were any of you.

420
00:28:34,673 --> 00:28:39,753
I'm afraid not. Given that the
poor lady passed away that same day,

421
00:28:39,753 --> 00:28:43,873
an incident of this sort
would have been reported to me,

422
00:28:43,873 --> 00:28:49,353
or to Mrs Hughes. That's right.
I see. Well, thank you very much.

423
00:28:53,233 --> 00:28:57,633
What were that about? She wanted to
know if anyone had posted a letter

424
00:28:57,633 --> 00:29:01,033
for Miss Swire.  Oh, I did that. Daisy?

425
00:29:01,033 --> 00:29:06,993
What did you say?  She asked me
to put it in the box in the hall.

426
00:29:08,593 --> 00:29:11,313
Why? What were you doing in her room?

427
00:29:11,313 --> 00:29:15,353
Making up the fire. We started
talking, she'd written a letter.

428
00:29:15,353 --> 00:29:19,433
She was ever so nice. I still
get  sad when I think about her.

429
00:29:19,433 --> 00:29:22,913
And it didn't occur to you
to tell me?  Tell you what?

430
00:29:22,913 --> 00:29:26,353
Never mind. I am grateful to you, Daisy.

431
00:29:26,353 --> 00:29:28,393
You cannot know how much.

432
00:29:30,113 --> 00:29:33,833
Well, this is the last of them.
I'm glad they've hurried it

433
00:29:33,833 --> 00:29:35,913
so she can be married from Downton.

434
00:29:35,913 --> 00:29:40,513
Are you? A little sober reflection
would not have gone amiss.

435
00:29:40,513 --> 00:29:42,913
Mama, let's try to be positive.

436
00:29:43,793 --> 00:29:48,033
Of all of them, Anthony is the
most traditional choice. Robert,

437
00:29:48,033 --> 00:29:51,713
Edith is beginning her
life as an old man's drudge.

438
00:29:51,713 --> 00:29:56,153
I shouldn't think a large
drawing room much compensation.

439
00:29:56,153 --> 00:30:00,713
Why dwell on that now? To have the
pleasure of saying, "Told you so."

440
00:30:03,073 --> 00:30:06,593
Now, the moment you
feel tired, you tell me,

441
00:30:06,593 --> 00:30:10,753
I'll take over whatever it is
you're doing. Oh, will you now?

442
00:30:10,753 --> 00:30:13,233
Are you sure you want
to come to the church?

443
00:30:13,233 --> 00:30:15,513
You could stay here and have a lie down.

444
00:30:16,513 --> 00:30:20,033
It would be so nice

445
00:30:20,033 --> 00:30:25,353
if people would wait to learn if I
really am ill before boxing me up.

446
00:30:25,753 --> 00:30:27,913
I don't know what you mean?

447
00:30:27,913 --> 00:30:30,753
I don't know anything about any illness.

448
00:30:30,753 --> 00:30:32,993
(SIGHS) Don't you?

449
00:30:33,873 --> 00:30:35,753
I see.

450
00:30:38,233 --> 00:30:41,233
Who told him? I don't know.

451
00:30:41,233 --> 00:30:45,153
Maybe he just picked it up
somehow. He's worried about you.

452
00:30:45,153 --> 00:30:48,313
He's a good man. He's a hopeless liar.

453
00:30:48,313 --> 00:30:51,153
That's quite nice, really, isn't it?

454
00:30:54,473 --> 00:30:56,953
I've had a message from the doctor.

455
00:30:57,313 --> 00:30:59,433
He'll have the results tomorrow.

456
00:31:00,113 --> 00:31:02,313
I'm to call in the afternoon.

457
00:31:02,313 --> 00:31:04,633
Try not to worry.

458
00:31:04,633 --> 00:31:08,393
(SIGHS) I'll try, but I won't succeed.

459
00:31:11,353 --> 00:31:13,393
(SIGHS)

460
00:31:13,393 --> 00:31:15,433
(DOOR OPENS)

461
00:31:15,433 --> 00:31:17,633
That's it, I'll put the hat on later.

462
00:31:17,633 --> 00:31:19,713
Go straight to Lady Edith.

463
00:31:19,713 --> 00:31:22,513
You look marvellous. I feel marvellous.

464
00:31:22,513 --> 00:31:26,873
That is, I feel marvellous because
we don't have to leave Downton.

465
00:31:26,873 --> 00:31:31,273
Lavinia did write to her father
and it was posted from this house.

466
00:31:31,273 --> 00:31:35,833
In other words, every word Mr
Swire wrote in that letter was true.

467
00:31:41,273 --> 00:31:43,993
(SIGHS) Daisy posted it.

468
00:31:43,993 --> 00:31:46,113
The kitchen maid.

469
00:31:50,273 --> 00:31:52,793
I see. Do you, my darling?

470
00:31:53,553 --> 00:31:57,473
I hope so, because if you
try to find one more excuse

471
00:31:57,473 --> 00:32:01,553
not to accept the money, I'll
have to beat you about the head.

472
00:32:03,913 --> 00:32:05,753
I see.

473
00:32:06,673 --> 00:32:08,873
(SIGHS)

474
00:32:08,873 --> 00:32:10,993
I do have one condition, however.

475
00:32:10,993 --> 00:32:14,753
Make it a good one. Let's
not steal Edith's thunder.

476
00:32:14,753 --> 00:32:18,793
I'll tell Robert after it's
over and she's left on honeymoon.

477
00:32:18,793 --> 00:32:20,793
Now, that I can live with.

478
00:32:39,314 --> 00:32:41,354
You look beautiful.

479
00:32:41,354 --> 00:32:44,834
All of us married. All of us happy.

480
00:32:45,914 --> 00:32:47,914
And the first baby on the way.

481
00:32:48,634 --> 00:32:53,634
Let's get a picture of the three
of us when we get to the church.

482
00:32:53,634 --> 00:32:57,714
He looks as if he's waiting for
a beating from the headmaster.

483
00:32:57,714 --> 00:33:00,234
Do you think I should reassure him?

484
00:33:00,234 --> 00:33:04,794
How? He's done it before so he must
be in possession of all the facts.

485
00:33:04,794 --> 00:33:09,114
Perhaps the first Lady Strallan
was a difficult act to follow.

486
00:33:09,114 --> 00:33:11,274
Or a difficult one to repeat.

487
00:33:17,394 --> 00:33:19,674
Well, fashionably late is one thing.

488
00:33:19,674 --> 00:33:24,554
Are we going in? Edith, I know
we haven't always got along,

489
00:33:24,554 --> 00:33:27,754
and I doubt things'll
change much in the future,

490
00:33:27,754 --> 00:33:30,994
but today I wish you all
the luck in the world.

491
00:33:32,034 --> 00:33:33,714
Thank you.

492
00:33:47,794 --> 00:33:49,754
Oh, look.

493
00:33:50,634 --> 00:33:52,474
Thank you very much.

494
00:33:58,874 --> 00:34:00,914
(ORGAN STARTS PLAYING)

495
00:34:25,874 --> 00:34:27,674
Good afternoon.

496
00:34:27,674 --> 00:34:29,674
Good afternoon, my sweet one.

497
00:34:42,194 --> 00:34:45,674
Dearly beloved, we are gathered...

498
00:34:45,674 --> 00:34:48,314
I can't do this. (ALL GASP) What?

499
00:34:48,314 --> 00:34:50,314
I can't do it.

500
00:34:53,314 --> 00:34:56,674
You know it's wrong, you
said so. My dear chap...

501
00:34:56,674 --> 00:34:59,434
No, I shouldn't have  let it get this far.

502
00:34:59,434 --> 00:35:03,314
I should've stopped it long
ago.  I tried to stop it.

503
00:35:03,314 --> 00:35:05,194
What are you saying?

504
00:35:05,194 --> 00:35:08,314
I don't understand what you're saying.

505
00:35:08,314 --> 00:35:10,154
Edith...

506
00:35:11,514 --> 00:35:15,754
Edith, I can't let you throw
away  your life like this.

507
00:35:15,754 --> 00:35:17,914
What do you mean?

508
00:35:18,914 --> 00:35:20,954
We're so happy, aren't we?

509
00:35:21,354 --> 00:35:25,114
We're going to be so
terribly, terribly happy.

510
00:35:26,394 --> 00:35:29,554
You are going to be happy,
 I pray that you are,

511
00:35:29,554 --> 00:35:32,034
but only if you don't
 waste yourself on me.

512
00:35:32,034 --> 00:35:34,194
Anthony, it is too late for this.

513
00:35:34,194 --> 00:35:36,474
Might I suggest we take a step back?

514
00:35:36,474 --> 00:35:40,154
No, let him go. Let him
go. You know he's right.

515
00:35:40,154 --> 00:35:44,314
Don't stop him doing the
only sensible thing in months.

516
00:35:44,314 --> 00:35:47,034
Thank you, Lady Grantham. But Granny!

517
00:35:47,034 --> 00:35:49,234
It's over, dear, don't drag it out.

518
00:35:49,234 --> 00:35:52,114
Wish him well and let him go.

519
00:35:52,114 --> 00:35:55,794
I can't.  Goodbye,  my dearest darling,

520
00:35:56,794 --> 00:35:58,834
and may God bless you...

521
00:35:58,834 --> 00:36:00,554
always.

522
00:36:01,354 --> 00:36:03,114
But...

523
00:36:23,594 --> 00:36:25,514
Oh, quick.

524
00:36:31,754 --> 00:36:33,754
(WEEPS)

525
00:37:01,514 --> 00:37:05,114
When everyone gets back,
can you clear all this away?

526
00:37:05,114 --> 00:37:09,154
I want it gone before Lady Edith
comes downstairs. Everything.

527
00:37:09,154 --> 00:37:14,034
Ask the outside staff to help put
back the carpet and the furniture.

528
00:37:14,034 --> 00:37:16,034
(DOOR OPENS)

529
00:37:18,794 --> 00:37:22,194
Is there anything I could
say to make it better? No.

530
00:37:25,794 --> 00:37:29,634
Look at them, with their husbands...

531
00:37:29,634 --> 00:37:33,474
Sybil pregnant, Mary probably pregnant.

532
00:37:33,474 --> 00:37:35,394
Just go!

533
00:37:36,194 --> 00:37:38,994
I mean it, go! Perhaps you should go.

534
00:37:43,634 --> 00:37:45,554
Oh, Mama.

535
00:37:47,314 --> 00:37:49,554
You are being tested,

536
00:37:51,994 --> 00:37:54,554
and do you know what they say, my darling?

537
00:37:56,194 --> 00:37:59,314
Being tested only makes you stronger.

538
00:38:00,794 --> 00:38:02,874
I don't think it's working with me.

539
00:38:51,154 --> 00:38:54,314
What shall we do now?
There's nothing we can do

540
00:38:54,314 --> 00:38:56,674
beyond removing all signs of a wedding

541
00:38:56,674 --> 00:38:58,994
and holding her hand while she recovers.

542
00:38:58,994 --> 00:39:01,194
She will, of course.

543
00:39:01,874 --> 00:39:05,954
Meanwhile, it's time to face
the business of leaving Downton.

544
00:39:05,954 --> 00:39:09,994
Without the wedding to hide behind,
there's no reason to delay it

545
00:39:09,994 --> 00:39:13,994
and astonish the world with the
extent of my wretched failure.

546
00:39:14,514 --> 00:39:16,514
Actually,

547
00:39:17,234 --> 00:39:21,754
Mary and I intended to make
an announcement at dinner.

548
00:39:21,754 --> 00:39:25,474
What announcement? What
about? You don't have to leave.

549
00:39:26,834 --> 00:39:28,834
I'll explain it later, but...

550
00:39:29,274 --> 00:39:32,114
I'm going to give you Reggie's money.

551
00:39:32,114 --> 00:39:35,834
I'll accept it. I'll give it to you.

552
00:39:39,274 --> 00:39:43,194
Don't be silly, you're not
going to give me any money.

553
00:39:43,194 --> 00:39:45,394
I am. You don't want to leave.

554
00:39:46,354 --> 00:39:48,274
Nor does Mary.

555
00:39:48,514 --> 00:39:50,594
Nor do any of us for that matter.

556
00:39:50,594 --> 00:39:52,794
I still won't take your money.

557
00:39:58,794 --> 00:40:02,594
What I will allow is for
you to invest in the place.

558
00:40:02,594 --> 00:40:06,594
If we stay, you'll share the
ownership, it'll be your house,

559
00:40:06,594 --> 00:40:09,914
your estate as much as mine.
We will be joint masters.

560
00:40:09,914 --> 00:40:14,034
And if you won't agree, I will
sell and it will all be your fault.

561
00:40:26,674 --> 00:40:30,314
I never thought I'd feel
sorry for an earl's daughter.

562
00:40:30,314 --> 00:40:33,154
All God's creatures have their troubles.

563
00:40:35,114 --> 00:40:37,394
Anna... Yes?

564
00:40:38,354 --> 00:40:42,194
Do you think it's right women
should say what they think?

565
00:40:44,234 --> 00:40:46,834
Speak out about romance and everything?

566
00:40:47,914 --> 00:40:53,034
Well, things are changing for
us and the vote won't be long now

567
00:40:53,034 --> 00:40:56,354
so they must get used
to us speaking our minds.

568
00:40:56,354 --> 00:41:00,234
But what? With most of
the men I've ever met,

569
00:41:00,234 --> 00:41:02,434
if you started to court them,

570
00:41:02,434 --> 00:41:04,874
they'd be so terrified they'd run a mile.

571
00:41:17,674 --> 00:41:22,514
Has she had something to eat?
Anna took up some sandwiches.

572
00:41:22,514 --> 00:41:24,914
She didn't touch a thing.

573
00:41:24,914 --> 00:41:30,234
That reminds me. Carson, I don't
want Edith to see any wedding food.

574
00:41:30,234 --> 00:41:34,394
Mrs Hughes and Anna are taking
what's left to Mr Travis tomorrow

575
00:41:34,394 --> 00:41:38,914
for the poor. If the poor don't
want it, bring it over to me.

576
00:41:41,474 --> 00:41:45,554
How can we help Edith? By
finding her something to do.

577
00:41:53,514 --> 00:41:56,514
Is this all we're
getting? The pickety bits?

578
00:41:56,514 --> 00:41:59,314
Hardly. These are canapes, Alfred.

579
00:41:59,314 --> 00:42:03,234
For your first course,
truffle egg on toast, perhaps?

580
00:42:03,234 --> 00:42:04,914
Oysters a la russe.

581
00:42:04,914 --> 00:42:08,594
Then what? There's lobster
rissoles in mousseline sauce.

582
00:42:08,594 --> 00:42:12,834
Or calvados-glazed duckling. Or
maybe a little asparagus salad

583
00:42:12,834 --> 00:42:15,274
with Champagne saffron vinaigrette.

584
00:42:15,274 --> 00:42:17,994
When I think how you've
gone to such pains...

585
00:42:17,994 --> 00:42:21,794
What about the pain of
that poor girl upstairs?

586
00:42:21,794 --> 00:42:25,674
Jilted at the alter... I
couldn't stand the shame.

587
00:42:25,874 --> 00:42:28,434
Then it's lucky no-one's ever asked you.

588
00:42:28,434 --> 00:42:33,194
Poor thing. How will she find
the strength to hold up her head?

589
00:42:33,194 --> 00:42:37,034
I'd have to run away and hide
in a place where no-one knew me.

590
00:42:37,034 --> 00:42:39,634
She's well out of it. How can you say it?

591
00:42:39,634 --> 00:42:42,074
She's young, she's not bad looking,

592
00:42:42,074 --> 00:42:45,714
she could do much better than
that broken-down old crock.

593
00:42:45,714 --> 00:42:49,154
Sir Anthony may have betrayed
a daughter of this house

594
00:42:49,154 --> 00:42:53,514
but he doesn't deserve to be
addressed like that by a footman.

595
00:42:53,514 --> 00:42:57,354
Oh, I think he does. Every
bit of that and worse.

596
00:42:57,354 --> 00:43:00,074
Well, maybe just this once.

597
00:43:00,074 --> 00:43:04,674
Right, what's it to be?
Lobster, duck or asparagus?

598
00:43:04,674 --> 00:43:06,594
Is there any cheese?

599
00:43:24,634 --> 00:43:26,954
What would you like me to get you?

600
00:43:26,954 --> 00:43:28,954
A different life.

601
00:43:32,194 --> 00:43:35,354
Let me bring you up some breakfast.

602
00:43:35,354 --> 00:43:37,114
No.

603
00:43:40,114 --> 00:43:42,394
I'm a useless spinster,

604
00:43:42,794 --> 00:43:46,194
good at helping out, that is my role,

605
00:43:47,074 --> 00:43:49,554
and spinsters get up for breakfast.

606
00:43:56,634 --> 00:43:58,634
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

607
00:44:02,594 --> 00:44:05,634
Going out? Just into the village.

608
00:44:05,634 --> 00:44:07,794
I... have to fetch something.

609
00:44:07,794 --> 00:44:09,794
Can I help?

610
00:44:09,794 --> 00:44:11,754
I'm going down later.

611
00:44:11,754 --> 00:44:13,714
No, thank you.

612
00:44:14,474 --> 00:44:17,314
This is an errand I have to do for myself.

613
00:44:17,314 --> 00:44:19,034
Ready?

614
00:44:19,794 --> 00:44:21,874
As ready as I'll ever be.

615
00:44:38,994 --> 00:44:40,994
(DOOR CLOSES)

616
00:44:48,154 --> 00:44:50,154
You know that's not true.

617
00:44:52,194 --> 00:44:54,314
You can be sure of one thing.

618
00:44:54,314 --> 00:44:56,594
I won't be cured by standing here.

619
00:45:31,514 --> 00:45:33,514
Do you want... No.

620
00:45:44,994 --> 00:45:46,994
Everything all right, Miss O'Brien?

621
00:45:50,874 --> 00:45:54,514
Oh, yes, everything's all right with me,

622
00:45:54,994 --> 00:45:59,034
but it'll be all wrong with you
before too long, mark my words.

623
00:45:59,034 --> 00:46:01,314
Oh? And how is that, Miss O'Brien?

624
00:46:01,314 --> 00:46:03,874
I don't know, not yet,

625
00:46:03,874 --> 00:46:06,274
but it will be.

626
00:46:06,274 --> 00:46:08,274
You can be sure of it.

627
00:46:17,434 --> 00:46:19,154
Well?

628
00:46:20,194 --> 00:46:24,794
Is it or isn't it? It's not cancer.
It's a benign something or other.

629
00:46:24,794 --> 00:46:26,514
Nothing more.

630
00:46:28,554 --> 00:46:31,194
Don't mention that you've said anything.

631
00:46:31,194 --> 00:46:33,234
She doesn't know that I know.

632
00:46:33,234 --> 00:46:35,114
I won't say a word.

633
00:46:41,114 --> 00:46:46,314
Did you tell him? I would prefer
to say I put him out of his misery.

634
00:46:52,874 --> 00:46:55,194
(MR CARSON SINGS)

635
00:46:55,194 --> 00:46:57,714
♪ Dashing away with the smoothing iron

636
00:46:57,714 --> 00:46:59,594
♪ She stole my heart away

637
00:46:59,594 --> 00:47:02,354
♪ Dashing away with the smoothing iron

638
00:47:02,434 --> 00:47:04,514
♪ Dashing away with the smoothing iron

639
00:47:04,594 --> 00:47:06,994
♪ Dashing away with the smoothing iron

640
00:47:06,994 --> 00:47:09,554
♪ She stole my heart away ♪

641
00:47:09,554 --> 00:47:11,274
Hm.

642
00:47:18,154 --> 00:47:20,874
I haven't had a letter
from Mr Bates in weeks.

643
00:47:20,874 --> 00:47:23,674
He wants me to make a new life without him.

644
00:47:23,674 --> 00:47:27,994
Am I to answer to you both? I have
made an investment. That's all.

645
00:47:27,994 --> 00:47:31,754
You abandon a pregnant woman in
a foreign land and run for it?!

646
00:47:31,754 --> 00:47:35,954
Other men have normal families.
No family is ever what it seems.

647
00:47:36,194 --> 00:47:39,434
Tell them I'm all right. Sybil? Hello?

648
00:47:40,314 --> 00:47:42,314
itfc subtitles

